// Forward Log-Polar Warp
vec2 logPolar(vec2 p) {
    float r = length(p);
    return vec2(log(r), atan(p.y, p.x)); //
}

Use code with caution.
The "SDF-Breaking" Trapped Origin
When you warp space logarithmically, you compress infinite space down into the center point. If you sample a standard texture or evaluate a fixed 3D SDF using these coordinates without a correction factor, the distance metric becomes non-linear. The raymarching engine will calculate incorrect step sizes, resulting in heavy glitching, edge tearing, or the ray falling straight through the geometry. 
